invariant: INV-22
file: session.c
catches: unit
reason: tlsi_fail answers the peer's fatal alert with one of its own, which
  RFC 9846 section 6.2 forbids: on a fatal alert both sides close the
  connection at once. A caller whose send holds only input during ch_read
  then sees a send it did not ask for. bin/unit requires the read that meets
  the peer's alert to make no send call.

--- old
    if (t->alert_received == 0) {
        t->alert_sent = description;
        (void)tlsi_send_alert(t, 2, description);
    }
--- new
    t->alert_sent = description;
    (void)tlsi_send_alert(t, 2, description);
